{"id":"word:hebrew:H5237","type":"word","title":"נׇכְרִי","subtitle":"H5237 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"strange , in a variety of degrees and applications ( foreign , non-relative , adulterous , different , wonderful )","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נׇכְרִי (H5237) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 46 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נׇכְרִי (nokrîy) means strange , in a variety of degrees and applications ( foreign , non-relative , adulterous , different , wonderful ) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 8 41."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נׇכְרִי","transliteration":"nokrîy","pronunciation":"nok-ree'","strong":"H5237","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5237","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["נָכְרִיָּֽה","נָכְרִיּ֑וֹת","הַ/נָּכְרִ֑י","נָכְרִיּ֛וֹת","נָכְרִ֔י"],"morphs":[["HAafsa",10],["HAafpa",9],["HAamsa",9],["HTd/Aamsa",5],["HTd/Aafpa",3],["HAampa",2],["HR/Aafsa",2],["HR/Aamsa",1],["HRd/Aamsa",1],["HC/Td/Aamsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"strange , in a variety of degrees and applications ( foreign , non-relative , adulterous , different , wonderful )","usage":"alien, foreigner, outlandish, strange(-r, woman).","full":"H5237. nokri נָכְרִי adjective foreign, alien (Late Hebrew נָכְרִי = Gentile ); — ׳נ absolute masculine Zeph 1:8 +; feminine נָכְרִיָּה Exod 2:22 +; masculine plural נָכְרִים Isa 2:6 2 t. + Prov 20:16 Kt (&gt; Qr נָכְרִיָּה ), + 27:13 (so read for נָכְרִיָּה ᵑ0 ); feminine plural נָכְרִיּוֺת Gen 31:15 +; — 1. a. foreign: נָכְרִי עַם Exod 21:8 (E) a foreign (non-Israel) people, נ ׳אִישׁ Deut 17:15 (|| אָתִיךָ לֹא ); נ ׳מַלְבּוּשׁ Zeph 1:8 ; נָכְרִיָּה אֶרֶץ Exod 2:22 (J) foreign land , so 18:3 (E); especially נָכְרִיּוֺת נָשִׁים foreign (non-Israel) women 1Kin 11:18 ; Ezra 10:2 , 10 , 11 , 14 , 17 , 18 , 44 ; Neh 13:26-27 ,. b. as substantive נָכְרִי foreigner (non-Israel) Judg 19:12 (+ יִשְׂרָאֵל מִבְּנֵי לֹא אֲשֶׁר ), 1Kin 8:41 (+ מֵעַמְּךָ לֹא אֲשֶׁר ), = 2Chr 6:32 (+ id. ), 1Kin 8:43 2Chr 6:33 ; Deut 14:21 (|| גֵּר ), 15:3 ; 23:21 (opposed to אָחִיךָ ), 29:21 (+ רְחוֺקָה מֵאֶרֶץ יָבאֹ אֲשֶׁר ); as predicate, 2Sam 15:19 (|| גֹּלֶה ), נָכְרִיָּה Ruth 2:10 ; plural נָכְרִים foreigners Lam 5:2 ( זָרִים ), Obadiah 11 (|| id. ); compare נָכְרִים יַלְדֵי Isa 2:6 ; feminine plural alien women Gen 31:15 (E; i.e. not of one's father's family). 2 נָכְרִיָּה foreign woman , as technical term, in Proverbs, for harlot (perhaps because harlots were originally chiefly foreigners): Prov 2:16 (|| זָרָה אִשָּׁה ), 7:5 (|| id. ), 5:20 (|| זָרָה ), 6:24 (|| רָ֑ע אֵשֶׁת ), 23:27 (|| זוֺנָה ). — On 20:16 ; 27:13 see below 3 figurative unknown, unfamiliar: בְּעֵינֵיהֶם הָיִיתִי נָכְרִי Job 19:15 an alien am I become in their eyes ; ׳נ אִמִּי לִבְנֵי Psa 69:9 (|| לְאֶחָ֑י הָיִיתִי מוּזָר ); נ ׳אִישׁ Eccl 6:2 ; of ׳י s judgment, עֲבֹדָתוֺ נָכְרִיָּה Isa 28:21 strange is his task! (|| מַעֲשֵׂהוּ זָר ); נָכְרִיָּה גֶּפֶן Jer 2:21 an alien vine (opposed to אֱמֶת זֶרַע ), figurative of degenerate Israel; as substantive, נָכְרִים Prov 20:16 Kt (&gt; Qr נָכְרִיָּה ), alens , persons unknown to him (|| זָר ), so read also (for נָכְרִיָּה ᵑ0 ) || 27:13 .","rootNote":"from 5235 (second form);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 8 41","keyReferences":["1Kgs 8 41","1Kgs 8 43","1Kgs 11 1","1Kgs 11 8","2Chr 6 32","2Chr 6 33","2Sam 15 19","Deut 14 21"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":46,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 8 41","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":41,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נָּכְרִ֔י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Aamsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 8 43","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":43,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/נָּכְרִ֑י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Aamsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 11 1","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָכְרִיּ֛וֹת",